                        "sense_id": "21eab18a-54c4-3999-894f-2be5e5b79c94",
                        "entry_id": "47ab91ed-10b8-37bd-8069-1fd8be61c130",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To go fishing for blackfish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "be462393-7879-4b59-9334-c00d26e883ff",
                                "sense_id": "21eab18a-54c4-3999-894f-2be5e5b79c94",
                                "text": "Earlier (Caldwell and Caldwell 1971a), we concentrated on the blackfishing at St. Vincent, the fishery with which we were most familiar, and listed known localities of fishing for blackfish and other species in the southern Caribbean."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e71ec5bb-01ae-4602-9089-ca607417c79d",
                                "sense_id": "21eab18a-54c4-3999-894f-2be5e5b79c94",
                                "text": "Long Island Sound, Block Island Sound, Rhode Island Sound, and Narragansett Bay have many spots where blackfishing is productive year after year."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81173a42-33ef-4ed4-8696-3637c89bd82d",
                                "sense_id": "21eab18a-54c4-3999-894f-2be5e5b79c94",
                                "text": "Blackfishing from the beach. I've done my research. Hundreds of shipwrecks line the Jersey coast, and many of them are close enough to reach with a long cast on a dead-low tide. These wrecks hold tautog, porgies, sea bass, flounder."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
